From adf6fff8b2565746e6051ab882e31974c4156c4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:37:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 105/125] decode-link: what the fuzzer and the comparison with
 podkop's shell decoder showed

- A parameter whose name grows when lowered (a letter of another alphabet after
  "sb.") was an index out of range: the path is now cut by what the name starts with.
- An option of a structure with several shapes (a transport, an obfuscation) is taken
  by the shape the structure has: one of another shape is "no such option" at once,
  not at the building of the outbound. A type named by a path is set before the rest.
- vcn gets a warning only when the certificate would be verified by another name than
  Xray verifies it by, and the warning says what follows; cs says what it is.

The fuzz target now holds, for any input: no message repeats the user of the link;
what is printed reads back and into the options of its type with no option the type
does not have; nothing a link may not set is in it. 10 million inputs in 150 s pass.

The decoder was also compared with the shell code of podkop over 1533 links: every
difference is one of the intended ones (uTLS chrome by default, TLS for Trojan,
allowInsecure, early data of WebSocket, httpupgrade and http transports, a "+" in a
password, IPv6 addresses, the links podkop made dead outbounds of).
